# the overload guard (engine.c engine_load), on synthetic loads ("load N": every block costs N % as the guard sees
# it): knit's unison never thins (the knob's count plays, whatever the load); the voice guard takes the pool to eight
# voices on sustained load and gives them back two a second
wait 300
load 40
preset 3 dusty_pad knit
param 3 e3 7
knob 3 vmode poly
play 3 G3 on
play 3 B3 on
play 3 D4 on
wait 500
expect voices 3
load 82
wait 1000
tap GLO
turn SELECT 5
wait 100
listen
where
unsaid saws
# the voice guard: one block over 92 % does not trip it (a spike: capping afterwards would not save it)
load 60
wait 2000
expect guard 16
load 98
wait 6
load 60
wait 500
expect guard 16
# three in a row do: eight voices; then, the average under 70 % with blocks of 90 % now and then (a song's
# spikes), two voices back each second
load 98
wait 25
load 60
wait 200
expect guard 8
load 90
wait 6
load 60
wait 1000
expect guard 10
wait 1000
expect guard 12
load 90
wait 6
load 60
wait 2000
expect guard 16
# a sustained 86 % trips it (the average) and holds it while it lasts
load 86
wait 1500
expect guard 8
wait 1500
expect guard 8
load 60
wait 4500
expect guard 16
play 3 G3 off
play 3 B3 off
play 3 D4 off
load 0
wait 500
